//
// smolvla profiling: compile then profile on NPU2, capturing the action-chunk
// latency into smolvla.perf.json via bench/extract_perf.py. Collected by the CI
// target check-programming-examples-llms-profile. Correctness is gated
// separately by run_npu2_verify.lit.
//
// This test exists so the nightly does not misreport the model. Its summary
// step emits a null-metric row for any model that passes verify but produces no
// profile record, on the assumption that its profile run failed; without this
// lit, smolvla would trip that path every night.
//
// SmolVLA is not autoregressive, so two of the three shared metrics do not
// apply. `ttft_ms` carries the action-chunk latency -- the time to the model's
// first usable output, which is what the field means for a policy that emits
// one (1,50,6) chunk instead of a token stream. `context_len` is the prefix the
// backbone attends over. `decode_tokens_per_sec` stays null: there is no decode
// loop to measure, and reporting a number there would invent one.
//
// Input is synthetic, matching run_npu2_verify.lit, so no dataset is fetched.
//
// Same weight features as the verify test, and no hf_token: both repos are
// public and ungated.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, lerobot, hfweights_lerobot_smolvla_base, hfweights_huggingfacetb_smolvlm2_500m_video_instruct
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_profile
// RUN: cd test_peano_profile
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile compile PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile profile PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | tee profile.txt
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/extract_perf.py profile.txt --model smolvla > smolvla.perf.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < smolvla.perf.json
// CHECK: "model": "smolvla"
